From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:39:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(reconciler): deploy inference services one phase per
 pass

The reconciler started an empty workflow and reported Ready=True right
away (also when the start failed), so a resource was "ready" without an
instance and nothing ever wrote status.endpoints.

ReconciliationController now drives an InferenceService through one
legal transition per pass and writes the phase back each time, with
Ready=False and the phase as reason until it is serving:

- Pending -> Scheduling once the policy allows the deployment (the
  policy is evaluated only when leaving Pending);
- Scheduling -> Preparing after allocate(); Preparing replays the
  allocation by its key and starts the deployment workflow with a
  LaunchRequest carrying the allocated devices -> Deploying;
- Deploying -> Verifying once launch-instance succeeded, and
  Verifying -> Ready when the run succeeded, writing status.endpoints
  from the launched instance and Ready=True. Passes in between poll
  find_run() every workflow_poll_interval seconds.

Only the passes that reach Ready or Failed return done=True, so the
dedup key of a generation never blocks the next pass. A workflow that
cannot be started or looked up keeps the phase and the allocation and
is retried with exponential backoff (WorkflowStartFailed /
WorkflowLookupFailed, capped at MAX_RETRY_DELAY_SECONDS). A failed,
cancelled or timed-out run moves the resource to Failed with the run's
error (WorkflowFailed) and releases the allocation unless the instance
may still be running; then deletion goes through Terminating and the
release provider stops it. A run that cannot be found any more
(WorkflowRunNotFound) also ends in Failed and keeps the allocation.
Failed is final: there is no automatic retry, and Ready resources have
no update flow yet.

A release provider is now required together with a workflow runtime
(DeploymentReleaser cancels the run and stops the instance on delete),
and resources other than InferenceService report NotDeployable.

The end-to-end tests run the controller manager, FirstFitScheduler,
LocalWorkflowRuntime and an in-memory launcher together: create ->
Ready with endpoints, restart and replay without a second instance or
allocation, a start failure retried, and a failed run or a deletion
during or after the deployment leaving no instance or allocation.
